<title>USA: Pakistan to import more wheat in 97/98 - US attache.</title>
<headline>Pakistan to import more wheat in 97/98 - US attache.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan will import an estimated 4.0 million tonnes of wheat in 1997/98, up 500,000 tonnes from previous estimates, according to a U.S. agricultural attache report made public on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The report also raised Pakistan's estimated wheat production for 1997/98 to 17.3 million tonnes, up 1.5 million tonnes, because of good weather and an increase in the average yield.</p>
<p>The Pakistan government plans to import 4 million tonnes of wheat for 1996/97. &quot;Large imports are required despite an increased production estimate of 17.3 million tonnes, 1.5 million tonnes more than the initial estimate,&quot; according to the report, dated July 2 and prepared by the U.S. embassy in Islamabad.</p>
<p>Provincial food departments have submitted cumulative requirement of more than 4.0 million tonnes for imported wheat, the report said.</p>
